{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lateralus feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's layered songs and shifting rhythms.",
    "Master of Puppets, City of Evil and The Art of Balance connect with my interest in heavy guitar music that also offers melody and detailed arrangements."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Vile feels too relentlessly brutal for what I want now; enjoying aggressive music does not mean aggression alone makes an album appealing.",
    "St. Anger's raw repetition misses the melodic and intricate qualities I am seeking, while American Idiot's punk-rock direction feels less relevant to my current heavier listening."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat heaviness as enough of a connection, even though melody, rhythm and song development affect my choices.",
    "My earlier accessible-rock listening seems to carry too much weight when my recent choices make intricate, heavier music more compelling today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interest in 10.000 Days makes another Tool album especially appealing because of its particular sound and arrangements.",
    "There is a difference between music that fits my taste and music I would choose now: Ride the Lightning, Cowboys from Hell and Dirt appeal to me, but feel less urgent than the strongest matches."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You understood my interest in heavy music, but my strongest choices depend on melody, intricate arrangements and a close connection to my recent listening."
}"}
